| 6 | Phase 1 negative path: digit cap keeps `#1234 seed data` firing; changing `\d{1,2}` to `\d+` ⇒ count 0. | CLI-executable | post-impl | `test "$(printf '#1234 seed data\n' \| bin/check-prose --stdin --chat \| grep -c bare-hash-ref)" = 1` |
| 7 | Phase 1 negative path: same-line real ref survives the exemption; the hit snippet names `#2453`. Anchoring the regex or wrapping the first branch so `search` skips the line ⇒ count 0. | CLI-executable | post-impl | `test "$(printf '#1 seed lost to #2453\n' \| bin/check-prose --stdin --chat \| grep -c '#2453')" = 1` |
