| 9 | Phase 1 negative path: `#2 in the queue` and `#12 in the stack` both fire (closed conference list); adding `queue` or `stack` to the list ⇒ count drops below 2. | CLI-executable | post-impl | `test "$(printf '#2 in the queue\n#12 in the stack\n' \| bin/check-prose --stdin --chat \| grep -c bare-hash-ref)" = 2` |
| 10 | Phase 1 boundary paths: `#1 seedling` and `backlog#12 seed` fire (word boundary; backlog branch untouched) while `#9 seed the DB` passes (accepted residual). Dropping the trailing `\b` or adding the lookahead to the backlog branch ⇒ count is not 2. | CLI-executable | post-impl | `test "$(printf '#1 seedling\nbacklog#12 seed\n#9 seed the DB before the run\n' \| bin/check-prose --stdin --chat \| grep -c bare-hash-ref)" = 2` |
| 11 | Phase 3: on-touch freshness passes for `.claude/rules/prose-style.md`; skipping the `last_verified` bump ⇒ exit 1 `body changed but last_verified not bumped`; a future date ⇒ exit 1 `last_verified in the future`. | CLI-executable | post-impl | `bin/check-docs --since=master --no-staleness` |
| 12 | Phase 3: the new Shape sentence carries no tell; writing it with a hanging dash ⇒ exit 1 `[em-dash]`. | CLI-executable | post-impl | `bin/check-prose --since=master` |
